// @check
// @error extern `logLine` takes `string`, which cannot cross a host boundary — an extern carries i32, i64, f32, f64 and boolean only; pass bytes as a `Buf`'s `base` and `length` (two i32s) and read them through the module's exported `memory`
// CONTRACT (must-error): the extern type set is closed to scalars, and the refusal names the
// workaround rather than the mechanism. A `string` is a WasmGC ref: it crosses to wasmtime,
// which can read GC objects, and is OPAQUE to a browser host, which cannot — so admitting it
// would make an extern portable to one host and not the other.
extern function logLine(s: string): i32

print(logLine("hi"))
